nd industry-engaged leader to shape real estate education in a city renowned for its dynamic commercial real estate market and historic appeal.The Buono E... View Details Bookmark Chair of the Engineering Department F2016457P Engineering Faculty The School of Engineering, Computing, and Mathematics (SECM) at the College of Charleston invites applications for a tenured position as Chair of the Department of Engineering at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor, with an anticipated start date of January 2026. Appointment rank and tenure status will be based on the candidate’s qualifications and experience.The successful candidate w... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of Mathematics F2016432P Mathematics Faculty 02/16/2026 The College of Charleston Department of Mathematics and Statistics invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position beginning August 2025. Candidates in applied mathematics, ideally ones with expertise in numerical analysis, are preferred. Applicants must possess a Ph.D. in mathematics or a mathematical science by the employment start date. Since teaching, research and servi... View Details Bookmark Engineering (Pool) Faculty Adjunct Faculty – EngineeringThe new and growing College of Charleston Department of Engineering invites applications for adjunct faculty to teach undergraduate courses in systems engineering, electrical engineering, and core engineering subjects. Areas of instructional need include:· Electrical and Mechanical Systems· Human Factors· Design and Development· Discrete Modeling and Simulation· Cir... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of Studio Art (Sculpture and New Media) F2016462P Studio Arts Faculty The Department of Studio Art at the College of Charleston invites applications for a tenure track Assistant Professor position in New Media & Technology with a Sculpture Focus, beginning August 2026. The successful candidate will have an MFA with a focus in sculpture and a secondary focus in new media. They will also have a demonstrated competency in computer-based fabrication and an intere... View Details Bookmark Instructor of Hebrew F2016471P Jewish Studies Faculty 12/15/2025 The Yaschik/Arnold Jewish Studies Program at the College of Charleston invites applications for a full-time position at the rank of Instructor of Hebrew beginning August 2026. We are seeking a dynamic and dedicated instructor with demonstrated excellence in teaching Modern Hebrew as a world language. The ideal candidate will also be interested and credentialed to teach interdisciplinary courses... View Details Bookmark Email: jobs@cofc.edu General Information: 843.953.5512 Mailing Address: 66 George St. Charleston, SC 29424 HR Office 160 Calhoun St. Lightsey Building B36 Charleston, SC 29424 Campus Maps ©2020 All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
